<title>UK: AEA Tech says Kvaerner group wins UK deal.</title>
<headline>AEA Tech says Kvaerner group wins UK deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Science and engineering company AEA Technology Plc said on Monday it was part of a Kvaerner-led consortium that won a 140 million stg contract to build a new plant for British Nuclear Fuels (BNFL).</p>
<p>AEA said its portion of the deal was worth about 7.0 million stg.</p>
<p>The contract is for an intermediate level radioactive waste encapsulation plant at BNFL's Sellafield site.</p>
<p>Other members of the group included Tarmac Plc and Design Group Partnership. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
